/*!
    \page tutorial-economy-and-bases.html
    \title Tutorial 9: Economy, Bases and the Radial Menu
    \previouspage {Tutorial 8: Selecting Units and Giving Orders}
    \nextpage {Tutorial 10: AI Opponents and Wildlife}

    \section1 Income

    Income is a scheduler event that repeats itself:

    \quotefromfile backend/game.cpp
    \skipto void game_t::schedule_income(
    \printuntil resource.amount_ += resource.income_;

    Old events check the match id and stop after a new match starts, so we do not have to
    cancel them by hand.

    The HUD shows a bar that fills until the next income. The core only sends a counter,
    QML animates the bar.

    \section1 What a base can do

    Units, research and upgrades come from data. A unit in \c data/base_types.json:

    \code
    {
      "creature": "orc_spearman", "tier": 2, "gold": 25, "food": 1, "timeMs": 12000,
      "training": { "gold": 30, "timeMs": 30000 }
    }
    \endcode

    Tier 2 units need base level 2 and a training research first. A research path in
    \c data/tech_tree.json:

    \quotefromfile data/tech_tree.json
    \skipto "id": "base_regeneration",
    \printuntil ]

    \section1 Orders

    Each action has its own queue in \l base_orders_t, so a base can research and produce
    at the same time. An order ends with a scheduler event:

    \quotefromfile backend/base_orders.cpp
    \skipto void base_orders_t::complete(
    \printuntil change_();

    If there is no free tile for a new unit, the order retries one second later.

    \section1 The radial menu

    Felgo has no radial menu, so we build one from a \c Repeater. Each circle goes on a ring
    around the base:

    \quotefromfile qml/components/RadialMenu.qml
    \skipto readonly property real angle:
    \printuntil y: radialMenu.height

    The progress ring is a Qt Quick \c Shape:

    \quotefromfile qml/components/ActionCircle.qml
    \skipto PathAngleArc {
    \printuntil }

    Research icons use Felgo \c AppIcon. Actions you cannot use yet turn grey with
    \c MultiEffect:

    \code
    MultiEffect {
        source: circleContent
        saturation: actionCircle.clickable ? 0 : -1
    }
    \endcode

    \b {Why not AppToolTip for the cost?} Felgo's \c AppToolTip is a tutorial overlay that
    dims the screen. A small \c Rectangle works better for hover tips.

    \image readme-base-menu.png
    \caption The radial menu with a unit queue and running research.
*/
